{"id": "EUVD-2026-53466", "enisaUuid": "3dfe8c2b-643d-3c79-9fb3-af8144c1c2fe", "description": "A vulnerability in the web-based management interface of Cisco IMC could allow an authenticated, remote attacker with&nbsp;Admin privileges to execute arbitrary commands on the underlying operating system of an affected system and elevate privileges to root.&nbsp;\r\n\r\nThis vulnerability is due to improper validation of user-supplied input. An attacker could exploit this vulnerability by entering crafted inputs to the web-based management interface of the affected software. A successful exploit could allow the attacker to execute arbitrary commands on the underlying operating system as the root user.&nbsp;\r\nCisco has assigned this vulnerability a SIR of High rather than Medium as the score indicates because additional security implications could occur when the attacker becomes&nbsp;root.", "datePublished": "2026-08-05T16:27:53", "dateUpdated": "2026-09-16T03:56:59", "baseScore": 6.5, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:H/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:N", "references": ["https://sec.cloudapps.cisco.com/security/center/content/CiscoSecurityAdvisory/cisco-sa-cimc-arg-inject-upSHdMfU"], "aliases": ["GHSA-424c-37gm-gvcf", "CVE-2026-20288"], "assigner": "cisco", "epss": 0.64, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0164261d-f1dc-3e2d-bfa5-4ea803a5a65b", "product": {"name": "Cisco Enterprise NFV Infrastructure Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "4.16.1"}, {"id": "017e8fe6-de8a-3493-aa63-2acd5a44bd56", "product": {"name": "Cisco Unified Computing System E-Series Software (UCSE)", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "3.2.7"}, {"id": "05a48c05-a091-30a0-aa10-7bc3c181240a", "product": {"name": "Cisco Enterprise NFV Infrastructure Software", "vendor": {"name": "Cisco"}}, "product_version": "4.4.1"}, {"id": "0839f2dd-285f-3a02-80e1-81ff096aa254", "product": {"name": "Cisco Unified Computing System (Standalone)", "vendor": {"name": "Cis